-- title:
--   Value of χ_A·|·|_A at det of Hecke generators
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a positive natural number, let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $n$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that for every $v \notin S$ the prime $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ does not divide the ideal generated by $n$. Consider the homomorphism $(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times} \to \mathbb{C}^{\times}$ given by the product of [`DirichletCharacter.dirichletIdeleChar`](def/DirichletCharacter_DirichletIdeleChar.html#L125) $\chi$ — the inverse of the composite of the unit-group homomorphism attached to $\chi$ with the residue homomorphism $(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times} \to \mathbb{Z}/n$ — and of the module character `MeasureTheory.distribHaarChar` of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, transported from $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{\times}$ into $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ along $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \to \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{C}$; precompose it with the determinant $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) \to (\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times}$. The assertion is that for every $v \notin S$, evaluating this homomorphism at the element `gen` $v$ of the carrier data `productionPinsCompact` $\mathbb{Q}$, whose generator field is the Hecke generator `heckeGen` at $v$ formed from the uniformiser unit at $v$, and reading the result in $\mathbb{C}$, gives $\chi(\mathrm{Nm}(v.\mathrm{asIdeal}) \bmod n) \cdot \mathrm{Nm}(v.\mathrm{asIdeal})^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{Nm}$ denotes the absolute ideal norm.
--
--   This records the Hecke eigenvalue normalisation of the central character data on the automorphic side: the idele class character attached to a Dirichlet character $\chi$, multiplied by the adelic modulus character, takes the value $\chi(\mathrm{N}v)\,(\mathrm{N}v)^{-1}$ at the determinant of the Hecke generator at each prime $v$ away from the level. It feeds the construction of the weight-one lift in the dihedral case, being cited in the statements about `smoothCuspRealizationAt` and `weightOneLift` for primitive forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_dirichletIdeleChar_mul_modulus_det_gen.lean

import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_ProductionPinsCompact
import Definitions.Def_DirichletCharacter_DirichletIdeleChar

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open NumberField AutomorphicForm
open IsDedekindDomain

theorem LanglandsTunnell.dirichletIdeleChar_mul_modulus_det_gen
    {n : ℕ} [NeZero n]
    (χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ n)
    (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)))
    (hS : ∀ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ), v ∉ S → ¬ v.asIdeal ∣ Ideal.span {(n : 𝓞 ℚ)}) :
    ∀ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ), v ∉ S →
      ((((DirichletCharacter.dirichletIdeleChar χ *
          (Units.map (Complex.ofRealHom.toMonoidHom.comp NNReal.toRealHom.toMonoidHom)).comp
            (MeasureTheory.distribHaarChar (AdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)).toHomUnits).comp
          Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.det) ((productionPinsCompact ℚ).gen v) : ℂˣ) : ℂ)
        = χ ((Ideal.absNorm v.asIdeal : ℕ) : ZMod n) * ((Ideal.absNorm v.asIdeal : ℕ) : ℂ)⁻¹ := by sorry
